WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:03.970
<v Examiner>The female sexual response, and four words.

2
00:00:04.420 --> 00:00:06.856
<v Examiner>Describe the female sexual response,

3
00:00:06.856 --> 00:00:11.931
<v Examiner>according to the effects of parasympathetic and sympathetic nerve impulses.

4
00:00:11.931 --> 00:00:17.007
<v Examiner>Then explain the terms menarche, menopause, amenorrhoea, and dysmenorrhoea.

5
00:00:17.457 --> 00:00:20.392
The last two points on her reproduction checklist.

6
00:00:20.392 --> 00:00:24.794
She marks the first one self-directed, and her quizzes barely touch either,

7
00:00:24.794 --> 00:00:27.377
so here's her slide, short and to the point.

8
00:00:27.827 --> 00:00:31.002
The female sexual response is similar to the male's.

9
00:00:31.002 --> 00:00:34.361
The clitoris and the vaginal mucosa engorge with blood,

10
00:00:34.361 --> 00:00:37.537
the same parasympathetic engorgement as an erection.

11
00:00:37.537 --> 00:00:42.239
The vestibular glands lubricate the vestibule, at the entrance to the vagina.

12
00:00:42.239 --> 00:00:46.637
Her slide notes the nipples harden under the sympathetic nervous system.

13
00:00:46.637 --> 00:00:52.072
Then orgasm, the sympathetic part: muscle tension, a faster pulse, higher blood pressure,

14
00:00:52.072 --> 00:00:54.515
and rhythmic contractions of the uterus.

15
00:00:55.965 --> 00:00:57.193
Now the four words.

16
00:00:57.193 --> 00:01:00.362
Menarche: the first menstrual period, at puberty,

17
00:01:00.362 --> 00:01:03.660
when the reproductive hormones first start surging.

18
00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:08.058
Menopause: the stage of life when the reproductive hormones decline,

19
00:01:08.058 --> 00:01:10.710
and the cycles become erratic, then stop.

20
00:01:10.710 --> 00:01:13.684
Amenorrhoea: the absence of menstrual periods.

21
00:01:13.684 --> 00:01:14.654
Think, no flow.

22
00:01:14.654 --> 00:01:16.659
Dysmenorrhoea: painful periods.

23
00:01:16.659 --> 00:01:18.599
Dys means bad, as in dyspnoea.

24
00:01:19.049 --> 00:01:21.867
And a bonus word from her slide: mittelschmerz,

25
00:01:21.867 --> 00:01:24.745
the twinge of pain some women feel at ovulation.

26
00:01:25.195 --> 00:01:25.746
<v Examiner>Once more.

27
00:01:25.746 --> 00:01:27.563
<v Examiner>The response, and the four words.

28
00:01:30.013 --> 00:01:32.899
The female sexual response is like the male's:

29
00:01:32.899 --> 00:01:38.168
the clitoris and vaginal mucosa engorge with blood, the vestibular glands lubricate,

30
00:01:38.168 --> 00:01:42.684
and orgasm brings muscle tension, a faster pulse, higher blood pressure,

31
00:01:42.684 --> 00:01:45.193
and rhythmic contractions of the uterus.

32
00:01:45.193 --> 00:01:47.012
Menarche is the first period.

33
00:01:47.012 --> 00:01:51.528
Menopause is when the reproductive hormones decline and the cycles stop.

34
00:01:51.528 --> 00:01:53.159
Amenorrhoea is no periods.

35
00:01:53.159 --> 00:01:55.229
Dysmenorrhoea is painful periods.
